            "review_text": "Go24209300430\n4 contributions\n0\nSlow service, Pathetic portion size, below average taste and quality in a five star hotel price\nMar 2024 • Couples\nI visited this restaurant tonight for dinner and to my surprise the food portion, taste and service, were all below average. I can say that because I have had Indian food in many Indian restaurants in Vietnam be it Hanoi, Hoi An and Da Nang, and all were good except this one. We went there seeing the reviews but it is definitely not recommend.\n\nWe ordered Masala Chai, Tomato Soup, Dahi Papdi Chat, Puri Bhaji & Veg Chowmein. We got Tea in the last. That to made my milk powder. It was very bad in taste. The tomato soup was cold when served. After complaining they got the same heated. You can imagine how freshly they cook the food. Now the portion was almost the size of a medium size tea cup. They served 6 Dahi Gol Gappe in the price of 150.000 VND. Only Two puris with the Bhaji. The taste was average but the price they charged for this slow service and pathetic portion food was more like a five star hotel. \n\nIf you want to try Indian Food in Da Nang, try other restaurants. There are plenty options. We had lunch in Gujarat Restaurant just around the road today and it was very nice. The taste, the quality, service, and price was reasonable too. Don't waste your time and money here.\nRead more\nWritten March 17, 2024",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
